    {
      "title": "2 · 🔴 SOURCE: req.query.sort",
      "description": "**Source:** the `sort` query parameter of `GET /orders`. Express 5's default query parser gives a string, or an array when the key is repeated.\n\n**Value here:** `sort = 'total'` for `GET /orders?status=open&sort=total` (example from docs/flows/list-orders.flow.json, not run).\n\n**Who can send it:** any user with a valid API token (step 3); no role is required.\n\n**Next →** checked? only `status` is (step 4); `sort` is passed on as `orderColumn` (step 5).",
      "file": "src/controllers/ordersController.js",
      "pattern": "const \\{ status, (sort) \\} = req\\.query",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 6,
          "character": 19
        },
        "end": {
