    {
      "title": "8 · ⚠️ SINK: ORDER BY ${orderBy}",
      "description": "**Sink:** `orderBy` is written into the SQL text of `pool.query` with a template literal. `$1` and `$2` bind `userId` and `status`; identifiers such as an ORDER BY column cannot be bound, so the text is used as-is.\n\n**Sink receives:** `... ORDER BY total` for `?sort=total`; `... ORDER BY created_at` with no `sort` (derived from code, not run).\n\n**Path summary:** A: `req.query.sort` (user, any logged-in user) → no check on `sort` → `ORDER BY` text. B: literal `'created_at'` → `ORDER BY` text.",
      "file": "src/repositories/orderRepository.js",
